  "summary": "SFist reports on crypto billionaire Chris Larsen's podcast interview with Kara Swisher, in which he said his son pressures him to stop funding SFPD's Flock surveillance technology. Larsen, who donated $9.4 million to SFPD's Real-Time Investigation Center in 2025, acknowledged growing backlash and suggested restrictions like shorter data retention periods.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "when Larsen told him that surveillance had helped bring crime down in San Francisco, his son responded that he would rather have the crime than the surveillance",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "SF currently retains Flock data for a year, far longer than the roughly 30-day period that had previously been Flock's standard \u2014 before Flock reduced it to seven days amid mounting criticism",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Florida ordered Flock license-plate readers removed from state highways last month, while Denver and Tempe, Arizona, have deactivated their cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
